// `.tutu` read straight into the tree the renderer indexes.
//
// The other way — `tutufile/lower` — prints each section as the text the old
// front end reads, and something re-parses it. That detour is where the
// fidelity bugs live: a printer holds the tree and loses it in the text, and
// every escape it forgets is a construct that silently changes meaning. This
// package skips it. Shrubbery in, `@anode.ANode` out, no string in between.
//
// Three things follow from going direct, and each is a DECISION rather than a
// consequence:
//
//   - A MACRO IS A TREE. `@anode.Macro` holds source text and re-parses it per
//     expansion, with `^name` substituted by the value parser. Here a macro
//     body is the shrubbery block it was read from, and expansion is a
//     substitution over `Ex` before anything becomes an `Expr`.
//   - WHITESPACE IS WHAT THE TREE SAYS. The HTML path inherits the tokenizer's
//     whitespace and then condenses it with a block/inline table
//     (`anode/whitespace.mbt`). At-notation has no such convention to inherit,
//     so nothing is inferred: a text node exists where the file writes one.
//   - THE EXPRESSION LANGUAGE HAS ONE READER. `Ex` (in `tutufile/lower`) is it.
//     What changes is only where it goes — `@tutuca.Expr` directly, rather than
//     tscript source that tscript parses back.
//
// It imports `tutufile/lower` for the reader and the `Ex` tree, and NOT for the
// printers. The printers are the thing being replaced; the equivalence tests in
// `to_expr_test.mbt` and `to_anode_test.mbt` are what say the replacement
// agrees with them, and they are the reason `lower` stays until stage 6 closes.
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/tutufile",
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/tutufile/lower",
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/tutufile/shrub" @sh,
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/core" @tutuca,
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/anode",
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/tscript",
  "marianoguerra/shrubbery/ast",
  "marianoguerra/error-report" @report,
}

import {
  "marianoguerra/shrubbery" @shrub,
  // The readers the printer path prints FOR. They are test dependencies only:
  // the equivalence tests are the whole reason `tutufile/lower` is still here,
  // and this package itself imports neither the printer's output format nor the
  // parsers that read it.
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/viewfile",
  "moonbitlang/core/debug",
} for "test"
